# The SQL migrations are hashed byte-for-byte by sqlx when they are applied, and
# those hashes are stored in the database. A Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` would rewrite every `\n` to `\r\n`, changing the hash of
# migrations that were already applied — sqlx then refuses to start, tauri's SQL
# plugin hands back no connection, and the app silently falls back to
# localStorage with the user's real database still on disk.
#
# Pinning the migrations to LF makes the bytes the app embeds the same on every
# machine, so a database migrated by one build is accepted by the next.
src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
